From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:04:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: Add Sony Xperia 10 VI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the Sony Xperia 10 VI (pdx246, codenamed columbia), the one device
shipping SM6450. Described so far: the debug UART, the PMIC complement
(PM6450, PM6150L, PMK8350 and PMR735A), the 45 RPMh-managed regulators
with the windows the board's own firmware uses, the power and volume
keys, the SD card slot with its card detect, and USB in OTG mode with
the high-speed PHY tuned the way the board's own firmware tunes it.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile             |   1 +
 .../sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts    | 412 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 413 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
